Well, I know this may sould strange from me, since I tend to like to keep
things the way they are(saves me time on the spoiler sheet.) but I have a new
idea for the next patch.  I have found that the whole concept of digging is
insanely easy if you get a pick axe.  What I mean is that there are no
inherant(sp???) dangers with the whole process.  The worst that can happen is
being jumped by a monster while digging.  Heck, once while I searched for a
vault (which I rarely do, money is usually not a problem) I just kept digging
in likely places while I looked for it, till I found it.  Now, what if I had
been digging, and I ran into ... 



A vein of molten lava, or perhaps a huge chasm.  You would just be working
along and get a message like, 'Seems a bit warm here' and you would have to
worry that you were getting close to a vein of lava.  You would have to
pick(oh, what a pun) and choose carefully.  Not only this, but if you DID
break into one, and happened to have fire resistance, you would fill part of
the level with molten lava, and you could run a chance of getting stone
resistance.  Of course, getting out of the hardened lava is a challenge, for
it would be very hard.  Heck, you could even have a lava lamp for an item.

With the chasm idea, perhaps it could span several levels, and even go through
some rooms.  There would be ropes that would let you put one down, and magic
ropes of climbing that would let you climb up one.  There would be monsters
that would attack you with the sole aim of knocking you off the ropes and to a
painful fall.  Perhaps a flying carpet which goes between levels.

Oh well, I never have posted my inane ideas, and since they probably reek, I
probably never shall again.  Boo-Hoo8-). 

Happy Hacking!

